  "answer_text": "In Massachusetts, the maximum amount you can collect in unemployment benefits depends on your weekly benefit rate, whether you have dependents, and the number of weeks you are eligible to receive benefits. \n\nThe maximum amounts are outlined below:\n\n### 1. Maximum Weekly Benefit Amount\n* **Base Maximum Benefit:** **$1,105 per week**. (This rate went into effect on October 5, 2025, and remains active through October 2026).\n* **Dependency Allowance:** If you have dependent children and are their main financial support, you can receive an additional **$25 per child per week**. \n  * *Note:* The total dependency allowance is capped at **50% of your weekly benefit amount**. (For example, if you qualify for the maximum $1,105 weekly benefit, your dependency allowance cannot exceed $552.50 per week).\n\n### 2. Maximum Duration (How many weeks you can collect)\n* **Maximum Duration:** **30 weeks**. \n  * While Massachusetts typically has a 26-week standard maximum, state law dictates that if the local unemployment rate in designated areas exceeds a certain threshold, the maximum is extended statewide to 30 weeks. This trigger was activated in April 2025 and remains in effect. \n\n### 3. Maximum Total Benefit Amount (Cap per benefit year)\nYour total benefit credit (the maximum amount you can collect in a 52-week benefit year) is capped at the **lesser** of:\n* **30 times your weekly benefit amount**, or\n* **36% of your total wages** earned during your base period (the last year of employment).\n\nIf you qualify for the maximum weekly benefit of $1,105 for the full 30 weeks, the maximum base payout is **$33,150** (excluding any added dependency allowances). \n\n---\n\n### How Your Specific Benefit is Calculated\nIf you do not qualify for the maximum cap, your personal weekly benefit is calculated as follows:\n* **Weekly Benefit Rate (WBR):** Roughly **50% of your average weekly wage** from your two highest-earning quarters during your \"base period\" (the last 4 completed calendar quarters before you file). \n* **Minimum Benefit:** The minimum weekly benefit rate in Massachusetts is **$98 per week**.",
